1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
这道东北菜，是为老外发明的
This Dongbei dish was invented for foreigners

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,400
1907年，哈尔滨道台府
1907, a Harbin official's kitchen

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,500
官厨郑兴文，专给外宾做菜
Chef Zheng Xingwen cooked for foreign guests

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,600
老外嫌咸鲜，想要酸甜
They found it too savory, wanted sweet-sour

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,800
他把咸味炸肉，改成糖醋
He turned salty fried pork sweet-and-sour

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,000
外壳酥脆，酸甜挂满汁
Crisp shell, glazed in sweet-sour sauce

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,200
本叫"锅爆肉"，被念成"锅包肉"
Named guo-bao-rou, misheard into today's name

8
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,300
尔滨人的骄傲，一咬咔嚓响
Harbin's pride — it crunches when you bite

9
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,500
番茄汁派，还是老式糖醋派
Ketchup style, or old-school vinegar style

10
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,700
一道菜，两派吵了快一百年
One dish, two camps, a century-long feud

11
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,900
为老外改的甜，成了东北的魂
Sweet made for foreigners became Dongbei's soul

12
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,000
你是番茄派，还是糖醋派？评论区见
Ketchup or vinegar — which are you?

13
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,200
下集：一口大铁锅，炖下整个冬天
Next: one iron pot, a whole winter inside
